<!-- ============ PROBLEM + REAL PROBLEM — combined ============ -->
<section id="problem" class="real bg-grid bg-grid-dark">
  <div class="wrap real-grid">
    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="sec-label">The problem</div>
      <h2>Your ministry is not the bottleneck. <em>Church admin</em> is.</h2>
      <p>You already know how to lead, teach and pastor. What slows you down is everything around it: replying to member queries, processing giving, evidencing safeguarding, coordinating volunteers, drafting responses and chasing missing items.</p>
      <div class="problem-cards">
        <div class="pcard">
          <span class="pcard-k">01 / Member care</span>
          <h4>Pastoral inbox</h4>
          <p>Prayer requests, counselling queries, family updates, urgent care.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pcard pcard-dark">
          <span class="pcard-k">02 / Compliance</span>
          <h4>Safeguarding &amp; DBS</h4>
          <p>Volunteer checks, training records, expiries, policy reviews.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pcard">
          <span class="pcard-k">03 / Giving</span>
          <h4>Donations &amp; Gift Aid</h4>
          <p>One-off, monthly, declarations, claims, reminders.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pcard pcard-lime">
          <span class="pcard-k">04 / Comms work</span>
          <h4>Member chase</h4>
          <p>Draft messages, emails, and follow-up replies.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="real-col">
      <div class="transcript reveal reveal-delay-2">
        <div class="sec-label">The real problem</div>

        <div class="transcript-stage">
          <img class="transcript-photo" src="/images/the-real-problem.png" alt="An exhausted pastor at a desk surrounded by paperwork and notes" />

          <div class="stage-overlay">
            <div class="stage-quote-wrap">
              <blockquote class="stage-quote">
                I feel like I'm working at <span class="hl">full capacity</span>, but I can't grow the ministry because admin eats my time.
              </blockquote>
              <div class="sig stage-sig">— Pastor using Zara Church Admin</div>
            </div>

            <div class="notes-wall" aria-hidden="true">
              <div class="note note-1">
                <span class="note-tape"></span>
                <p>"Prayer request came Friday. We replied Wednesday. Lost the moment."</p>
                <span class="note-attr">— Vicar, Birmingham</span>
              </div>
              <div class="note note-2 note-lime">
                <span class="note-tape"></span>
                <p>"Safeguarding pack is 9 fields per volunteer. Miss one, the rota stops."</p>
                <span class="note-attr">— Children's lead, Bristol</span>
              </div>
              <div class="note note-3">
                <span class="note-tape"></span>
                <p>"Replying at 11pm. My family sees me less than my email."</p>
                <span class="note-attr">— Senior pastor, Manchester</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="body-txt">
          The admin around each ministry sets the cap. <strong>More members means more pastoral replies to write</strong>, more giving forms to chase, more safeguarding to track, more events to coordinate. So the team either stops growing the ministry, or takes it on and pays for it with evenings and weekends.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

